    sign: [['Tracks', '3 to 3¼ in long, blocky heart shape; a buck track is wider with blunt tips, splayed on soft ground. Dewclaws show only in mud.'], ['Droppings', 'Clumped pellets in spring and summer (soft feed), separate pellets in winter; a pile the size of a fist is a mature deer.'], ['Rubs', 'Shredded bark on juniper and mesquite trunks the size of your wrist, September through January.'], ['Beds', 'Oval depressions 3 ft long on benches under a canopy, often two or three together on a point.'], ['Browse line', 'Clipped twig ends with a rough tear (no upper incisors).']],
    tactics: ['Glass from a point with the sun behind you: dawn on west-facing slopes, evening on east-facing. 10x binoculars on a tripod, then a 15x or spotting scope to judge.', 'Pick apart shade. A bedded buck shows as a horizontal line, an ear flick or an antler tine in a shadow.', 'Still-hunt north faces midday with the wind in your face when the glassing dies.', 'After a monsoon storm or snow, deer feed all day; after a cold front they feed hard the evening before.', 'Rut: find does. Bucks cover ground; sit above a doe group and wait.'],
    calling: ['Rattling and a grunt tube pull desert bucks in late December and January, especially with a decoy on open ground.', 'A fawn bleat stops a walking doe and the buck behind her.'],
    judging: ['Ears tip to tip on an alert desert buck are about 20 to 22 in; a buck with antlers well outside the ears is 26 in plus.', 'Count fronts: a true 4x4 with deep forks front and back, mass carried to the tips and eye guards is a mature buck.', 'Body: swayback, a sagging belly, a thick neck and a gray face say 5 years plus.'],
    shotNotes: ['Broadside: one third up the body, 3 to 4 in behind the front leg crease, through both lungs.', 'Quartering away: aim at the far front leg; quartering toward: wait.', 'Deer drop at the shot (archery): aim low third so a ducking buck still takes lungs.'],
    after: ['Mark the shot location and the last-seen spot before you move.', 'Give a lung-hit buck 30 minutes, a liver hit 3 hours, a gut hit overnight if weather allows.', 'Desert deer in August: gutless method and quarters in the shade within an hour, then ice.'],
    rules: ['Big-game draw (deer, fall turkey, fall javelina, bighorn, fall bison, sandhill crane) typically closes the first week of June; results in July.', 'Over-the-counter archery deer nonpermit tags in many units in August to September and December to January, with unit harvest limits that close units midseason: check the AZGFD closures page before each trip.', 'Validate the tag immediately (notch date and time) and attach it to the carcass; keep evidence of sex and species attached as the regs require.', 'CWD: head-drop barrels in northern units; carcass import from other states is restricted.'],
