    tactics: ['September: locate bugling bulls at first light from a ridge, then close to within 100 yards with the wind before you call, or slip in silent and let the herd come to you.', 'Set up on the downwind edge of a wallow or tank midday during a hot, dry rut.', 'Rifle: find the sanctuary. Draw a one-mile circle from every open road; the timber inside the gaps is where bulls live after opening day.', 'Glass P-J breaks at dawn in November and December from a mile away, then plan a stalk with the thermals (down in the morning, up after the sun hits).', 'After a snow, cut fresh tracks on roads and follow them into the timber with the wind.'],
